(THG-75: a WHOLE thing may be copied into a nested field, and between two
 fields of the same thing, and onto itself - all three are assignment
 (LANGUAGE.md:1121, 1139-1140), and delivery.vox:50 relies on the first.
 No example in this section shows any of them.
 The self-copy cases (`Set span's start to span's start.`, `Set twin to
 twin.`) are the memory-safety edge: an overlapping copy of a run of bytes
 onto itself. Both are safe here.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox THG-75.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   3
   8
   8
   8
)
A thing called point has
  a number called x is 0,
  a number called y is 0.

A thing called segment has
  a point called start,
  a point called end.

a point called anchor.
Set anchor's x to 3.
a segment called span.
Set span's start to anchor.
Print span's start's x.
Set span's end's y to 8.
Set span's start to span's end.
Print span's start's y.
Set span's start to span's start.
Print span's start's y.
a segment called twin is span.
Set twin to twin.
Print twin's start's y.
